From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:16:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] urlmon: Seek, IStorage binding, URL moniker methods, feature
 controls, error paths

Seek on the file, mk, http, ftp, gopher and bind protocols; BindToStorage(IStorage) for compound files; status codes of custom protocols reach the client; IMoniker IsRunning/GetTimeOfLastChange/ParseDisplayName of URL monikers; HlinkSimpleNavigateToString through the hyperlink frame; CoGetClassObjectFromURL and FaultInIEFeature for installed classes; per-thread and per-zone feature controls and the registry query; ZoneManager FixUnsecureSettings; IBinding GetBindResult across apartments; callbacks of URLOpenStream/URLOpenPullStream/URLOpenBlockingStream live as long as the bind; failed FTP connections end the bind (wininet reports the failure of an asynchronous InternetOpenUrl); UrlCombineW no longer writes into the caller's relative URL.

diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/path.c b/dlls/kernelbase/path.c
index bc51e9d..41421bc 100644
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/path.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/path.c
@@ -4934,11 +4934,18 @@ HRESULT WINAPI UrlCombineW(const WCHAR *baseW, const WCHAR *relativeW, WCHAR *co
     relative.cbSize = sizeof(relative);
 
     /* Get space for duplicates of the input and the output */
-    preliminary = heap_alloc(3 * INTERNET_MAX_URL_LENGTH * sizeof(WCHAR));
+    preliminary = heap_alloc(4 * INTERNET_MAX_URL_LENGTH * sizeof(WCHAR));
     mbase = preliminary + INTERNET_MAX_URL_LENGTH;
     canonicalized = mbase + INTERNET_MAX_URL_LENGTH;
     *preliminary = '\0';
 
+    /* The scheme of the relative URL is lowercased below: that has to happen on a
+     * copy, the caller's string may be read-only. */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_URLMON_COMBINE
+    lstrcpynW(canonicalized + INTERNET_MAX_URL_LENGTH, relativeW, INTERNET_MAX_URL_LENGTH);
+    relativeW = canonicalized + INTERNET_MAX_URL_LENGTH;
+#endif
+
     /* Canonicalize the base input prior to looking for the scheme */
     myflags = flags & (URL_DONT_SIMPLIFY | URL_UNESCAPE);
     len = INTERNET_MAX_URL_LENGTH;
